WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.005 --> 00:00:17.973
I was the first woman president

00:00:19.805 --> 00:00:21.465
of an African nation.

00:00:23.719 --> 00:00:30.203
And I do believe more countries
ought to try that.

00:00:30.227 --> 00:00:31.440
(Laughter)

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:38.464
(Applause and cheers)

00:00:39.292 --> 00:00:42.498
Once the glass ceiling has been broken,

00:00:44.482 --> 00:00:48.140
it can never be put back together --

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:52.440
however one would try to do that.

00:00:54.439 --> 00:00:59.280
When I assumed the presidency of Liberia

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.836
in January 2006,

00:01:06.062 --> 00:01:12.112
we faced the tremendous challenges
of a post-conflict nation:

00:01:13.366 --> 00:01:15.097
collapsed economy,

00:01:16.907 --> 00:01:18.788
destroyed infrastructure,

00:01:20.129 --> 00:01:22.724
dysfunctional institutions,

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.193
enormous debt,

00:01:26.603 --> 00:01:28.888
bloated civil service.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:31.570
We also faced

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:38.094
the challenges of those left behind.

00:01:39.392 --> 00:01:45.304
The primary victims of all civil wars:

00:01:46.175 --> 00:01:48.860
women and children.

00:01:51.298 --> 00:01:54.314
On my first day in office,

00:01:56.695 --> 00:01:57.973
I was excited ...

00:02:00.315 --> 00:02:01.831
and I was exhausted.

00:02:04.331 --> 00:02:08.140
It had been a very long climb

00:02:10.055 --> 00:02:11.698
to where I was.

00:02:14.549 --> 00:02:20.239
Women had been those who suffered most

00:02:21.335 --> 00:02:23.105
in our civil conflict,

00:02:24.229 --> 00:02:28.072
and women had been the ones to resolve it.

00:02:31.272 --> 00:02:33.518
Our history records

00:02:35.702 --> 00:02:38.430
many women of strength and action.

00:02:39.502 --> 00:02:45.565
A President of the United Nations
General Assembly,

00:02:45.589 --> 00:02:49.978
a renowned circuit court judge,

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:53.676
a president of the University of Liberia.

00:02:58.223 --> 00:03:04.235
I knew that I had to form

00:03:04.259 --> 00:03:06.831
a very strong team

00:03:08.466 --> 00:03:12.147
with the capacity to address

00:03:12.171 --> 00:03:15.720
the challenges of our nation.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:22.902
And I wanted to put women
in all top positions.

00:03:24.672 --> 00:03:28.632
But I knew that was not possible.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:36.428
And so I settled for putting them
in strategic positions.

00:03:38.027 --> 00:03:43.852
I recruited a very able economist
from the World Bank

00:03:43.876 --> 00:03:47.142
to be our minister of finance,

00:03:47.166 --> 00:03:49.937
to lead our debt-relief effort.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:56.444
Another to be the minister
of foreign affairs,

00:03:56.468 --> 00:04:03.052
to reactivate our bilateral
and multilateral relationships.

00:04:04.463 --> 00:04:07.423
The first woman chief of police

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:12.910
to address the fears of our women,

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:17.267
who had suffered so much
during the civil war.

00:04:18.321 --> 00:04:22.834
Another to be the minister of gender,

00:04:22.858 --> 00:04:28.168
to be able to ensure the protection
and the participation of women.

00:04:29.574 --> 00:04:31.686
Over time,

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:34.042
the minister of justice,

00:04:34.066 --> 00:04:35.937
the minister of public works,

00:04:35.961 --> 00:04:37.959
the minister of agriculture,

00:04:37.983 --> 00:04:40.525
the minister of commerce and industry.

00:04:44.125 --> 00:04:47.402
Participation in leadership

00:04:47.426 --> 00:04:51.513
was unprecedented in my administration.

00:04:53.656 --> 00:04:56.853
And although I knew

00:04:56.877 --> 00:05:02.647
that there were not enough women
with the experience

00:05:02.671 --> 00:05:06.599
to form an all-women cabinet --

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:08.821
as I wanted --

00:05:09.954 --> 00:05:14.481
I settled to appoint numerous women

00:05:14.505 --> 00:05:17.371
in junior ministerial positions,

00:05:18.416 --> 00:05:20.488
as executives,

00:05:20.512 --> 00:05:23.320
as administrators,

00:05:23.344 --> 00:05:25.304
in local government,

00:05:26.989 --> 00:05:28.785
in diplomatic service,

00:05:28.809 --> 00:05:30.831
in the judiciary,

00:05:30.855 --> 00:05:33.171
in public institutions.

00:05:36.165 --> 00:05:37.458
It worked.

00:05:39.387 --> 00:05:43.069
At the end of 2012,

00:05:45.898 --> 00:05:51.668
our economic growth
had peaked at nine percent.

00:05:55.213 --> 00:06:01.419
Our infrastructure was being
reconstructed at a very fast pace.

00:06:02.756 --> 00:06:06.744
Our institutions were functioning again.

00:06:08.387 --> 00:06:14.629
Our debt of 4.9 billion

00:06:14.653 --> 00:06:16.717
had been largely canceled.

00:06:18.302 --> 00:06:22.666
We had good relationships
with the International Monetary Fund,

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:23.841
the World Bank,

00:06:23.865 --> 00:06:25.963
the African Development Bank.

00:06:27.057 --> 00:06:31.461
We also had good working relationships

00:06:31.485 --> 00:06:34.438
with all our sister African countries

00:06:34.462 --> 00:06:37.803
and many nations all over the world.

00:06:39.372 --> 00:06:45.421
Our women could sleep
peacefully at night again,

00:06:45.445 --> 00:06:46.793
without fear.

00:06:48.345 --> 00:06:52.178
Our children were smiling again,

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:59.757
as I promised them during
my first inaugural address.

00:07:01.843 --> 00:07:06.740
The reputation and credibility

00:07:06.764 --> 00:07:08.819
of our nation,

00:07:08.843 --> 00:07:11.801
lost in the many years of conflict,

00:07:11.825 --> 00:07:13.039
were restored.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.412
But progress is never guaranteed.

00:07:18.673 --> 00:07:21.999
And in our legislature, in my first term,

00:07:22.023 --> 00:07:23.872
women were 14 percent.

00:07:24.655 --> 00:07:26.619
In the second term,

00:07:26.643 --> 00:07:30.862
it declined to eight percent,

00:07:30.886 --> 00:07:35.662
because the environment
was increasingly toxic.

00:07:37.821 --> 00:07:42.208
I had my fair shares
of criticism and toxicity.

00:07:43.409 --> 00:07:45.472
Nobody is perfect.

00:07:47.096 --> 00:07:52.513
But there's nothing more predictable

00:07:52.537 --> 00:07:54.293
than a strong woman

00:07:56.071 --> 00:08:00.658
who wants to change things,

00:08:02.218 --> 00:08:04.091
who's brave to speak out,

00:08:05.297 --> 00:08:07.563
who's bold in action.

00:08:09.992 --> 00:08:11.902
But I'm OK with the criticism.

00:08:13.514 --> 00:08:16.547
I know why I made the decisions I made,

00:08:16.571 --> 00:08:20.529
and I'm happy with the results.

00:08:21.775 --> 00:08:27.106
But that's why more women
leaders are needed.

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:34.087
For there will always be those
who will tear us down,

00:08:34.111 --> 00:08:36.496
who will tear us apart,

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:40.924
because they want
the status quo to remain.

00:08:43.373 --> 00:08:49.650
Although sub-Saharan Africa
has had major breakthroughs

00:08:49.674 --> 00:08:54.888
in women's leadership and participation,

00:08:56.396 --> 00:09:00.481
particularly in the legislature --

00:09:00.505 --> 00:09:04.658
in parliament, as it's called --

00:09:04.682 --> 00:09:06.056
so many women,

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:09.552
50 percent and over, one of our nations,

00:09:09.576 --> 00:09:14.454
well over 60 percent,
the best in the world --

00:09:14.478 --> 00:09:16.701
but we know that's not enough.

00:09:18.029 --> 00:09:24.175
While we must be very thankful

00:09:24.199 --> 00:09:26.627
and applaud the progress we have made,

00:09:27.668 --> 00:09:31.508
we know that there is much
more work to be done.

00:09:33.032 --> 00:09:38.198
The work will have to address
the lingering vestiges

00:09:40.309 --> 00:09:42.428
of structural ...

00:09:44.302 --> 00:09:46.199
something against women.

00:09:47.837 --> 00:09:51.254
In too many places,

00:09:51.278 --> 00:09:53.305
political parties

00:09:54.715 --> 00:09:58.644
are based on patronage,

00:09:59.945 --> 00:10:01.112
patriarchy,

00:10:02.477 --> 00:10:04.966
misogyny

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:08.622
that try to keep women

00:10:08.646 --> 00:10:12.086
from their rightful places,

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.751
that shut them out

00:10:14.775 --> 00:10:18.967
from taking leadership positions.

00:10:21.544 --> 00:10:25.552
Too often, women face --

00:10:27.067 --> 00:10:30.104
while the best performers,

00:10:30.128 --> 00:10:34.010
while equal or better in competence --

00:10:34.034 --> 00:10:35.564
unequal pay.

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:41.127
And so we must continue to work

00:10:41.151 --> 00:10:42.756
to change things.

00:10:44.202 --> 00:10:48.670
We must be able to change
the stereotyping.

00:10:50.516 --> 00:10:55.207
We must be able to ensure

00:10:55.231 --> 00:10:58.460
that those structural barriers

00:10:58.484 --> 00:11:01.407
that have kept women

00:11:01.431 --> 00:11:07.255
from being able to have the equity
they rightfully deserve.

00:11:08.229 --> 00:11:12.307
And we must also work with men.

00:11:14.206 --> 00:11:17.947
Because increasingly,

00:11:17.971 --> 00:11:20.936
there is recognition

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:23.976
that full gender equity

00:11:25.413 --> 00:11:29.635
will ensure a stronger economy,

00:11:33.317 --> 00:11:34.913
a more developed nation,

00:11:36.792 --> 00:11:38.760
a more peaceful nation.

00:11:40.785 --> 00:11:45.133
And that is why we must continue to work.

00:11:46.218 --> 00:11:49.623
And that is why we're partners.

00:11:51.535 --> 00:11:57.265
I will be launching a Center
for Women and Development

00:11:58.884 --> 00:12:00.649
that will bring together --

00:12:00.673 --> 00:12:06.990
(Applause)

00:12:08.319 --> 00:12:13.732
women who have started

00:12:13.756 --> 00:12:18.905
and are committed
to their joining of leadership.

00:12:20.613 --> 00:12:25.708
With women who have excelled

00:12:25.732 --> 00:12:32.263
and advanced in leadership together.

00:12:34.274 --> 00:12:36.424
Over a 10-year period,

00:12:37.923 --> 00:12:41.217
we strongly believe

00:12:41.241 --> 00:12:46.812
that we will create this wave of women

00:12:48.494 --> 00:12:53.017
who are prepared to take,

00:12:54.208 --> 00:12:55.787
unabashedly,

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:02.598
intentional leadership and influence

00:13:02.622 --> 00:13:04.340
throughout society.

00:13:07.085 --> 00:13:08.260
This is why --

00:13:10.411 --> 00:13:12.095
(Laughs)

00:13:12.119 --> 00:13:14.698
at 81, I cannot retire.

00:13:15.135 --> 00:13:16.669
(Applause and laughter)

00:13:16.693 --> 00:13:23.693
(Applause and cheers)

00:13:23.941 --> 00:13:28.052
Women are working for change

00:13:29.428 --> 00:13:30.578
in Africa.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:35.878
Women are working for change

00:13:37.278 --> 00:13:38.966
throughout the world.

00:13:41.556 --> 00:13:44.587
I will be with them,

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:47.857
and one of them,

00:13:49.234 --> 00:13:50.384
forever.

00:13:51.041 --> 00:13:56.945
(Applause)

00:13:56.969 --> 00:14:00.064
Thank you for listening.

00:14:00.972 --> 00:14:03.940
Go out and change the world.

00:14:03.964 --> 00:14:10.587
(Applause and cheers)

